    "name": "Chief Minister's Free Cancer Chemotherapy Scheme",
    "slug": "cmfccs",
    "description": "The scheme \"Chief Minister's Free Cancer Chemotherapy Scheme\" was launched by the Department of Health & Family Welfare, Government of Arunachal Pradesh on 1st of August 2017 to tackle the growing incidences of cancer in the state. Under this scheme, cancer patients will be provided the commonly used medicines for the treatment of the disease free of cost with a ceiling of ₹10.00 lakh per person per year.\nObjective:\nTo reduce the burden of high expenditure on cancer patients. To provide free chemotherapy for all types of cancer at any stage. Important Features: A Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) has been signed with TATA Memorial Hospital Mumbai for procurement of all the medicines at a concessional rate which will be provided to an upper limit of 1000 patients per year.\n\nEligibility criteria from source:\n1. Regular State Government Employees and their dependents are eligible for the scheme.\n\nBenefits from source:\nMedicine worth ₹10.00 lakhs per person per annum (₹5.00 lakh for 6 months).Free ConsultationFree counselingThe benefit of the scheme can be availed during the period of the entire treatment.\n\nApplication process from source:\nMode: OfflineStep 01: The applicant may visit the nearest State Tertiary Cancer Centre and also contact the Nodal Officer for the scheme.Step 02: Application in the prescribed format may be received from the concerned State Tertiary Cancer Centre.Step 03: The applicant must ensure that the filled information should be correct before submitting the application form to the concerned department.Step 04: After successful verification, the applicant can avail the benefit of the scheme.\n\nDocuments listed by source:\n• Identity proof\n• i.e. Aadhaar Card, Voter ID card, etc. Schedule Tribe Certificate for APST patientsTwo passport\n• size photographsAddress\n• proof\n\nFrequently asked questions from source:\nQ: What is the objective of the scheme?\nA: The objective of the scheme is to reduce the burden of high expenditure of cancer patient and provide free chemotherapy for all type cancer at any stage.\nQ: By which department was this scheme launched?\nA: Department of Health & Family Welfare, Government of Arunachal Pradesh When was this scheme launched\nQ: Understanding (MoU) signed?\nA: MoU has been signed with TATA Memorial Hospital Mumbai for procurement of all the medicines at a concessional rate.\nQ: Who is eligible under this scheme?\nA: The regular State Government Employee and their Dependents are eligible to apply under the scheme.\nQ: How many patients can take the benefits of this scheme?\nA: 1000 patients per year can take the benefits of this scheme.\nQ: What is the benefit of this scheme?\nA: Under this scheme, cancer patients will be provided the commonly used medicines for treatment of the disease free of cost with a ceiling of ₹10 lakh per person per year.\nQ: What are the other benefits to be provided to the cancer patients?\nA: Other benefits such as free consultation and free counselling can also be availed by the cancer patient.\nQ: Till when a patient can avail of the benefit of this scheme?\nA: The benefit of the scheme can be availed during the period of entire treatment.\nQ: How can I apply under this scheme?\nA: The applicant can visit nearest State Tertiary Cancer Centre and also contact the Nodal Officer for the Scheme.\n\nVerification note: this record came from a third-party structured extract. Confirm eligibility, benefit amounts, documents, application steps, and current status on the linked official page before advising a citizen.",
