    "name": "Mamata Scheme",
    "slug": "mamata",
    "description": "To alleviate the issue of maternal and infant undernutrition, Government of Odisha launched Mamata scheme in 2011 for pregnant women and lactating mothers. It is a conditional cash transfer maternity benefit scheme where Rs 5000/- is transferred to the bank account of mothers. Pregnant and lactating women of 19 & above age group, for the first two live births except those who avail maternity benefit (who are themselves employees or wives of employees of State Govt/Central Govt/PSUs). This scheme provides monetary support to the pregnant and lactating women to enable them to seek improved nutrition and promote health seeking behavior.\n\nEligibility criteria from source:\nPregnant and lactating woman of 19 & above age group, for the first two live births except those who avail maternity benefit (who are themselves employees or wives of employees of State Govt/Central Govt/PSUs).\n\nBenefits from source:\nTo provide partial wage compensation for pregnant and nursing mothers so that they are able to rest adequately during their pregnancy and after delivery. To increase utilization of maternal and child health services, especially antenatal care, postnatal care and immunization. To improve mother and child care practices, especially exclusive breastfeeding and complementary feeding of infants.\n\nApplication process from source:\nMode: Offline In order to get the benefit of Odisha Mamata Yojana, The beneficiary is required to register at Anganwadi centers and mini Anganwadi centers to which the beneficiary belongs.\n\nDocuments listed by source:\n• Aadhar\n• card. Residence certificate. Photocopies of MCP card. Self\n• declaration form. Bank account details. Passport size photograph. Mobile\n• number. Ration card.\n\nFrequently asked questions from source:\nQ: Is this scheme a Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT) Scheme?\nA: Yes. Are applications for this scheme open throughout the year\nQ: What is the First Instalment?\nA: (Rs.3000/-).Waht is Second Instalment\nQ: Receive IFA tablets?\nA: Through ANM by using MCP Card and MCTS/RCHS.\nQ: how to get counseling session?\nA: Receive at least one counseling session at the AWC/Village Health and Nutrition Day (VHND)/Home Visit by Scheme and ICDS Register.\nQ: How to get Child BCG vaccination?\nA: By ANM through MCP Card, MCTS/RCHS.\nQ: How to get Child Polio-1 & 2 & 3 vaccination?\nA: By ANM through MCP Card, MCTS/RCHS.\nQ: How to get Child Rotavirus 1 & 2 & 3 vaccinations?\nA: By ANM through MCP Card, MCTS/RCHS.How to receive\nQ: Child Mealses vaccine before attaining 1 year of age?\nA: By ANM through MCP Card, MCTS/RCHS.How to get more details about\nQ: Mamata Scheme?\nA: To get more details, Please visit https://wcd.odisha.gov.in/ICDS/mamata\n\nVerification note: this record came from a third-party structured extract. Confirm eligibility, benefit amounts, documents, application steps, and current status on the linked official page before advising a citizen.",
