    "name": "Bhagini Prasuti Sahayata Yojana",
    "slug": "bpsy",
    "description": "Chhattisgarh State Government bought the \"Bhagini Prasuti Sahayata Yojana\" for pregnant women. Under this scheme, pregnant women will get the financial assistance that will help her during the pregnancy expenses .\n\nEligibility criteria from source:\nApplicant should be a permanent resident of Chhattisgarh. Benefit will only be provided for only first two children. Benefit will only be provided to registered women. Registration as a construction worker is required one year in advance. It is mandatory to have authorized verification of pregnancy of the female worker by a doctor, ANM or Mitanin. Maternity assistance benefits will not be provided to the spouse of a construction worker employed in public and government institutions. Construction worker beneficiaries without valid Board membership will not qualify for the Maternity Assistance Scheme benefits.\n\nBenefits from source:\nFinancial Assistance : ₹ 10,000/-\n\nApplication process from source:\nMode: Offline Firstly, Applicant have to register at labor office of the area. Get the application form and full fill the form with required detailsAttach the required documents. The application will have to be submitted within the time limit to same office.\n\nDocuments listed by source:\n• Birth certificate of the child. A scanned copy of the registration certificate. Mobile Number. Aadhaar Card. Self\n• declarationBank\n• passbook photo copy.\n\nFrequently asked questions from source:\nQ: What is this scheme?\nA: Chhattisgarh State Government started a scheme \"Bhagini Prasuti Sahayata Yojana\" for pregnant women.\nQ: What is the benefits under this scheme?\nA: Financial benefits are provided.\nQ: What is the monetary sum offered or provided?\nA: mount : ₹ 10,000/-Who will get the scheme benefits\nQ: May other state women get the benefits?\nA: No, this is only for Chhattisgarh State.\nQ: How late can a applicant apply for the scheme?\nA: pplicant can apply up to 90 days after the birth of the childFor how many children can the applicant avail the benefit of this scheme\nQ: How will the beneficiary get the benefit?\nA: Beneficiary will get the benefit through the RTGS/NEFT in her bank account.\nQ: Who will get the benefit if a woman dies during childbirth?\nA: Benefits will be provided to her husband.\nQ: What documents are required for registration?\nA: Birth certificate of the child. A scanned copy of the registration certificate. Mobile Number. Aadhaar Card. Self-declaration. Bank passbook photo copy.\n\nVerification note: this record came from a third-party structured extract. Confirm eligibility, benefit amounts, documents, application steps, and current status on the linked official page before advising a citizen.",
